  "instance_name": "Cinco_de_Mayo",
  "label": "Cinco de Mayo",
  "description": "A real-world holiday celebrated on May 5th in Mexico and by Mexican communities around the world, commemorating the Mexican army's unlikely victory over the French Empire at the Battle of Puebla. It is often celebrated with parades, food, and music, particularly in the United States. The meme misrepresents this holiday by altering its name to imply a connection to Puerto Rico, which is a U.S. territory, thereby mocking or trivializing the cultural significance of the original holiday.",
